      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::web::015::thermal_stability_and_applicability_to_n"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing produces a contiguous and stable oxide layer at the interface between the HEA coating and Q235 steel.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited diffusion of reactive elements during annealing causes selective oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective oxidation forms a continuous and structurally robust oxide barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8779564::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide barrier suppresses further deleterious diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide barrier suppresses dissolution or dealloying.",
